    {
      "type": "generalise",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "prose": "Each time, you changed a number by $d$ to make it round, then undid the change. $$a + b = a + (b + d) - d$$ $$a - b = a - (b + d) + d$$ Added too much: take it off. Took away too much: give it back.",
      "question": "For $92 - 47$ you take away 50. What next?",
      "widget": {
        "kind": "choice",
        "layout": "stack",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "Add 3",
            "correct": true
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "Take away 3",
            "why": "You treated it like an addition. Taking away 50 removed 3 too many, so give 3 back."
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "Add 7",
            "why": "You used the units digit of 47. The gap from 47 up to 50 is 3."
          }
        ]
      },
      "hints": [
        {
          "rung": "nudge",
          "text": "Is 50 more or less than 47?"
        },
        {
          "rung": "step",
          "text": "$92 - 50 = 42$, and giving 3 back makes 45."
        }
      ],
      "feedback": {
        "correct": "$92 - 50 + 3 = 45$.",
        "generic": "Not quite right. Taking away 50 removed more than 47."
      },
      "explain": {
        "text": "Taking away 50 removed 3 more than 47. Adding 3 back gives $42 + 3 = 45$. Check: $45 + 47 = 92$."
      }
    },
